<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.12.4: Writing Equations in Different Forms</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00268</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.12.4: Writing Equations in Different Forms</md:title>
    <md:uuid>87b0cdee-14e3-46ed-9e61-cbe3ffd10b5e</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001"><emphasis>Three Different Forms of Linear Equations</emphasis></para>
      <para id="para-00002">Work with a partner to answer 1 - 3.</para>
      <!--Q#1-->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">What is the slope-intercept form of a linear equation?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q#2-->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00006">What is the point-slope form of a linear equation?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msub><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msub><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q#3-->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00009">What is the standard form of a linear equation?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>C</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <para id="para-00012"><emphasis>Using the Different Forms to Write Equivalent Equations</emphasis></para>
      <para id="para-00013">Linear equations can be written in the different forms to create linear equations. Use the linear equation forms from 1 - 3 to help you complete the rest of the activity. Remember to show all of your work on your paper and to use inverse operations to move terms to different sides of the equation.</para>
      <para id="para-00014">For 4 - 5, use the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <!--Q#4-->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00015">Write the equation in slope-intercept form.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00016">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q#5-->
      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00018">Write the equation in standard form.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00019">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Q#6-->
      <exercise id="exer-00006">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00021">Write <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in slope-intercept form.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00022">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00023"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>6</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> orb <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001">
      <para id="para-00024">Which of the following is equivalent to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in standard form?</para>
    </note>
    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>
      <section id="sect-00003">
        <title>Writing Equivalent Linear Forms</title>
        <para id="para-00025">Write an equation of a line in all three forms that has a slope of 2 and a <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of 7.</para>
        <para id="para-00026"><emphasis>Slope-Intercept Form</emphasis> Slope-intercept form is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> where m is the slope and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept. Substitute <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> to have the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00027"><emphasis>Standard Form</emphasis> Write the same equation in standard form. Standard form is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>B</m:mi><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>C</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00028">Remember that <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> can not be negative and there should not be any fractions or decimals.</para>
        <para id="para-00029">For this form, rearrange slope-intercept form to lead with the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> term:</para>
        <para id="para-00030"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Bring the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> terms on the left side. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00031"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Simplify. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00032"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Divide all terms by -1 so that <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>A</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is not negative. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00033"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Simplify. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00034"><emphasis>Point-Slope Form</emphasis> Point-Slope form is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msub><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:msub><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. Substitute the slope in for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and the point in for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msub><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:msub><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>m</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msub><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msub><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:msub><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00035">Notice this can easily be written in slope-intercept form by solving for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>:</para>
        <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00037"><emphasis>Standard Form to Slope-Intercept Form</emphasis> Standard form can also be rearranged into slope-intercept form.</para>
        <para id="para-00038">Write <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in slope-intercept form. Work to solve for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00039"><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - Bring the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> term to the right side with the constant. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>14</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00040"><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - Simplify. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>14</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00041"><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - Divide by the coefficient of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.  <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <para id="para-00042"><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - Simplify and write in the correct order. <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        <note class="try" id="note-00002">
          <title>Try It: Writing Equivalent Linear Forms</title>
          <!--Q#-->
  <exercise id="exer-00007">
            <problem id="prob-00007">
              <para id="para-00043">Write the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>24</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> in slope-intercept form.</para>
            </problem>
            <solution id="sol-00007">
              <para id="para-00044">Compare your answer: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
              <para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>24</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mn>24</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>24</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mtd></m:mtr><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="right"><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="center"><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mtd><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:math></para></solution>
          </exercise>
          <!--Interaction End --></note>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>